WEBVTT

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.870
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.160
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.190
Is today's episode about Nagihiko-san?

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:13.470
All kinds of things about Nagi's past will be revealed!

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.100
How embarrassing! {squee is a sound, and a gross word, and eww, please don't make us sub it}

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.820
New Guardian Characters, new Character Transformations... What more could you want? {non-literal. literally: "a whole extra helping!"}

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.990
A new Guardian Character? Wow, cool!

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.920
Doki!

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:43.180
If you were to walk so the wind fluttered the edge of your cape,

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:49.570
people would look up at you in quiet admiration.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:56.870
You can say spicy things like "it's not my style," if you want,

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:03.290
but I know who you really are because I'm your friend!

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.160
Stand! Bow!  {these are the two things said by the class rep when the teacher enters at the start of the school day}

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.690
Nice and orderly now!

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:10.530
And once that's done,

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:15.800
it's time to start the school day.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:23.420
I like Mondays because I can see all my friends.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:29.820
There's nothing wrong with being abnormally happy.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:36.990
At lunch break, we have tea in the Royal Garden,

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:44.330
where I tell you all my secrets!

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:11.980
Nadeshiko-san, you must be ever mindful that your actions are feminine.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.880
Even at school, you must learn alongside the other girls and model their mannerisms.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.910
Hey, what should we play during lunch break?

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.270
I'm sick of playing cat's cradle.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.860
Run, run!

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.110
Mach 2!

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.870
Mach 3!

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.450
You are the heir to the Fujisaki Household, after all.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.000
Yes, ma'am.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:39.510
Episode 91
Full Throttle! My Rhythm!

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:58.220
Kirishima-kun sure is popular.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:01.880
Starting to regret turning him down?

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:02.740
Not really...

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.600
Why don't you wave to him?

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.600
Amu!

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.440
Thanks for waiting! {he's filling in on the basketball team... This was mentioned back in a previous episode that Nagihiko does this}

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.170
Oh, sorry about this, Fujisaki.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.110
I'm happy to help. Anytime.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:21.960
Huh? Why is Nagihiko playing?

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:27.640
Oh, the basketball team has some injured players, so he's filling in for the next exhibition game.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.360
Weak! Keep loungin' around and I'll be sinking all the baskets!

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.150
Yo!

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:49.660
Here I come, Kiseki!

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.890
Just try to breach my ironclad defense!

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.130
Ran!

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.060
Dunk!

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.470
Yay!

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.100
Sheesh, this is your fault, Kiseki.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.660
It sure is-dechu.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:12.140
Ah, this place sure relaxes me.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.730
Why'd you come today?

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:18.840
As the former Jack, I came to see if the new Jack's doing his job.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.400
Does Fujisaki have any issues?

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.310
Issues?

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.160
He does his work way faster than you did, Kukai.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.910
And he's very attentive.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.870
Jack! Massage the King's shoulders!

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:37.470
And he's quite skilled at serving the King.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.800
Frankly, I think you're the loser Jack, Kukai.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:47.280
So that's that. Guess you don't have anything to worry about, Mr. Loser Jack.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.390
Well, don't you think so very highly of yourself!

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.790
Not really.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:57.400
Fine then, I'll teach you the Jack's true struggle!

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.060
You and me! It's on!

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.400
Loser buys ice cream! Got it?

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.450
Okay!

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.200
Ready, fight!

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:14.940
I'll show you the power of your senpai!

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.790
Be gentle.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:18.790
You can do it, Nagi!

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.540
Kukai, get in the spirit!

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.720
Wow...

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.590
What?

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.170
All right!

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.460
And the winner is: Kukai! A word, if you please.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.630
This is the power... of your senpai.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:09.900
It seemed pretty close to me.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:14.730
Darn... I thought I almost had it.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:17.600
It was a good fight! You did great, Nagi!

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.780
Although you do happen to look just like Nadeshiko...

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.020
...you really are a boy after all, you know?

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:25.900
Fujisaki, let's get that ice cream!

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.480
Okay, okay...

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.720
Amu-chan, did something happen?

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.630
Uh, yeah...

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.640
I've been dying to try the banana kind.

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.600
You sure you don't want me to treat you?

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.170
Well, consider it a gift from your elder Jack.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:52.760
So tell me, what's the real reason you came?

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:53.430
Huh?

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.320
You didn't actually come by just to check up on me, did you?

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:02.470
Come on, do you honestly take me for someone with a hidden agenda?

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:05.650
I just came to see you.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.550
To see if the new Jack had found the answer to his question yet.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.390
The answer?

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:15.780
I have no idea...

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:21.740
While studying abroad, I discovered how many different types of dancing exist in this world,

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:27.440
and became lost in the feeling of how truly small the world of my traditional Japanese dance is.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:33.670
And then Temari went back in her egg and a new egg was born...

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:40.260
I thought I could find the answer if I continued to live as a boy, but...

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.740
So no change, then?

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:48.570
Well, it's best not to think too hard about it and just have fun, right?

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:53.070
If you keep doing what you wanna do, like that arm wrestling match we just had,

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.700
you'll find the answer sooner than you think.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.330
Fujisaki-kun's Guardian Egg?

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:00.950
Yeah.

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:06.810
I didn't notice one bit, you know?

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:07.980
Yeah...

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.280
You sure?

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.530
You can be a bit unreliable, you know.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.200
I saw it! I really did!

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.750
Hey, Tadase-kun, what kind of Guardian Character do you think is in Nagihiko's Guardian Egg?

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:21.150
We won't know that until it hatches, obviously.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:26.650
Whoever hatches from the egg is "the person he wants to be," at least.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.350
But what if the egg doesn't hatch?

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:35.150
I suppose that means there's still something he doesn't fully understand.

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.640
Amu-chan, over there!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.310
Nagihiko!

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:47.130
My Guardian egg?

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:51.570
Yeah, it looked like it moved a little. Can I take a look?

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:52.450
Sure.

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:55.260
So?

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.150
No... It hasn't...

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:00.640
...really changed at all.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.530
I guess you were just seeing things.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:09.480
Sorry, my bad!

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.270
Ah, it's you guys!

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:14.720
"You guys?"

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:16.640
Takashi!

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:17.500
Akira!

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.460
Keisuke!

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:20.560
Together we're:

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.210
Urban Street!

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:24.040
A comedy trio!

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:28.140
We're the best three-on-three basketball team!

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:30.030
They don't look like...

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.750
...the best to me.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:36.180
You know them?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.260
Huh? No...

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:42.160
What's coming over me?

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:11.380
Whoa!

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:13.110
Now...

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:13.750
Right!

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.490
This feeling...

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:25.530
It's finally finished!

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:28.180
We've analyzed the sound from Ikuto-kun's violin

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:31.770
and created a device that can reproduce that power electronically!

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:33.180
We call it the:

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.120
Come Here Embryo!

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:40.740
Now we can cause a vast number of X Eggs to gather, without Ikuto-kun!

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.780
Excellent. Test it out immediately!

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.660
Go, Come Here Embryo!

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:56.300
How is Ikuto?

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.200
He is still sleeping. {funny thing... I didn't realize this, but these people really are labeled in the script as "Black Cloths", so me calling them Men in Black is entirely correct}

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:03.060
It seems he will need more time before he will be able to play the violin again.

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:16.040
This egg is trying to hatch.

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:26.180
What is it? Have you discovered something about your lifestyle, Nagihiko?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:29.960
Yes.

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.310
Nagi's egg moved?

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:46.180
Yeah, it was clattering back and forth.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:49.950
Neat. So Nagi's going to be a Character Bearer soon.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.890
Nagihiko, what are you feeling right now? {like a sportscaster, call back to earlier}

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:53.900
Yaya-chan...

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:57.770
Hey, come on out! It's fun!

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:00.860
I wonder if he's shy?

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:03.780
How dare a commoner make his King wait!

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.860
You're all pitiful-dechu.

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:09.590
Let me handle this-dechu.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:11.490
That's some confidence you have.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:13.600
Pepe-chan, you can do it!

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:16.000
The whole world is watching you! {still in sportscaster mode, I guess}

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.640
I know-dechu.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:20.480
The egg is like a baby Guardian Character,

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:24.950
so a baby character like me should be able to reach him-dechu!

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.640
Come on out-dechu! Come on out-dechu! Come on out-de-

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:32.520
Don't fall asleep!

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.080
That was pointless.

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:38.410
Well, it's almost time for the game.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:41.460
Oh yeah, today's that exhibition game.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:42.340
Yeah.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:45.350
Good luck! We'll handle things here.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:48.480
Sorry, guys. I'll leave things here to you.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:51.300
Sure you don't want to go cheer him on, Rima-tan?

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:53.540
Kirishima-kun's gonna be there, too, right?

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.720
I have Guardian work to do. {jeeze, Yaya, get a clue. She's just not that into him.}

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.780
I'll handle it, really!

00:12:57.780 --> 00:12:58.520
I'm good.

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:03.250
Rima-tan, you're so stubborn. You should just be honest with yourself and-

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:04.850
I'm sowwy... {unless you're adamant about sworry...}

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:09.630
Huh? Nagihiko's uniform?

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:13.440
Thanks, Amu-chan.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:16.080
No problem, I'm glad I made it in time.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.140
You made an amazing shot yesterday!

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:24.710
D-D-D-Don't be s-s-scared, Takashi-kun!

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:27.740
That's right! We're the red-hot players:

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:30.300
Urban Street!

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.220
Hey!

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:32.120
Oh, sorry.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:35.620
You know them?

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:40.000
Where have I seen those three before?

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:45.680
How's it going?

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:47.180
Quite a lot are gathering. {referring to the people at the basketball match, I think}

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:49.930
Perfect conditions for a field test!

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:52.040
All right! Get it started!

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:53.410
Um...

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.720
What is it?

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.410
Where's the "on" button?

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:00.890
I forgot to install one... {so much for this sub-plot}

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:13.120
You can do it! Go! Go! {finally, Ran is cheering in a completely appropriate context! A broken clock is right twice a day, I guess}

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.610
We're already ten points down.

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:17.190
Are we gonna lose?

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:22.090
Don't give up! Play hard right till the end!

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:25.820
Of course!

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:27.330
It was back then!

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:31.130
Okay! Here we go! {damn, I guess they had a switch}

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:45.860
That sound!

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:02.220
Kirishima-kun!

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:03.590
Nagihiko!

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:19.670
That's...

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.220
Um...

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:23.130
Who are you again? {the X eggs are from the "urban street" boys}

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:27.650
I know I've seen you somewhere before...

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:30.360
Is that... X-1-san?

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:33.600
No, it's X-2-san!

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:34.990
Isn't it X-3-san?

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.830
X Characters!

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:43.210
What, they want us to play basketball?

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.330
Amu-chan, let's do this!

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:49.130
Okay!

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:55.390
My heart: Unlock!

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:16.400
Character Transformation: Amulet Heart!

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:27.840
Apparently, if we get it in that thing over there, we win.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.580
Amu-chan!

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.510
Right!

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:33.880
Start the game!

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:05.040
Wow, it's almost like he's dancing...

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:09.430
Right! I don't have to worry anymore!

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:13.880
Today, we're going to measure your vertical jump height.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:20.250
I have to make sure I only go as high as an average girl... I have to seem like a girl or else...

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:25.460
I wish I could jump as high as I want...

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:33.900
Here, I can forget being a girl.

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:36.840
And just go all out!

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.250
Whoa! {yup, they're in the flashback}

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:47.910
You can jump really high!

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:48.870
What's your name?

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.790
Huh? N-Nagi...

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:53.270
Nagi, huh?

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:55.470
Join our team!

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:57.050
Let's play basketball together!

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:06.600
Run as hard as I can... Jump with all my might...

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:11.770
The things I had to forget in order to dance like a girl...

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:16.360
But I don't have to worry about that anymore!

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:24.780
I'm a boy now and can go all out. I'll grab hold of my rhythm!

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:34.840
Your rhythm definitely reached me.

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:41.420
A Guardian Character?

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:46.310
I'm Rhythm! Come on, let's go!

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:52.020
My heart: Unlock!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:10.830
Character Transformation: Beat Jumper!

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:20.180
This is...

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:27.730
Not fair!

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:31.590
Make it cool, Nagi!

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:32.310
Okay!

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.280
Wow!

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:44.160
Beat Dunk!

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:55.870
Please don't feel so down.

00:19:55.870 --> 00:20:00.130
If you have fun and don't give up, you're sure to get better someday!

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:03.420
Amu-chan, Open Heart!

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:04.300
Right!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:08.600
Negative Heart: Lock On!

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:14.440
Open Heart!

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:41.600
What about the Embryo?

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:44.720
It seems the output from the device was too weak.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:46.240
Dang...

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:57.730
Huh? What were we...

00:20:57.730 --> 00:20:59.020
Are you okay?

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:04.310
You... Are you... Nagi?

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:12.930
I'm sorry I forgot you!

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.750
Don't worry, it's not important.

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:20.030
He's late...

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:21.680
What's the matter?

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:29.300
We were only together for one day, after all.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:31.780
Let's play basketball together again sometime.

00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:32.860
Sure!

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:34.550
Then, all together now:

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:36.180
Urban Street!

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:38.190
That's not gonna happen.

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:43.030
I'm so happy. Nagihiko is a Character Bearer now, too!

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:48.910
So Ran, Miki, Su... You're all with Amu? I like your rhythm.

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:51.040
You're all so cute!

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:56.130
You think?

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:00.870
Whatcha think about this pose?

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:02.050
Like this, right?

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:03.610
No, like this?

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:13.080
I'm Rhythm! I've always got a cool beat heatin' up my heart! Nice to meet you!

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.200
Nice to meet you... {heart thump thump}

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:15.160
Miki...

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:16.600
Not again...

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:33.250
You sure do seem determined.

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:39.300
So even if you screw up, it'll somehow turn out all right.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:46.670
How about you just trust in yourself?

00:22:46.950 --> 00:22:53.130
Take that first step and everything will work out fine.

00:22:53.740 --> 00:23:00.060
Even if people see through your cool exterior, keep marching on.

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:09.140
Look up at the blue sky and everything will reset!

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:12.780
Take it easy! Take it easy!  {the first is in English, the second is in Japanese (but that is the exact same meaning)}

00:23:13.060 --> 00:23:23.320
Try to relax those shoulders and clear your mind.

00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:30.030
The more you do it, the easier it'll get, so keep taking it easy.

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:35.230
Ride the flow of time and you'll be...

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:39.030
Shining! Shining! Shining!

00:23:50.890 --> 00:23:52.690
Rhythm is so cool...

00:23:52.690 --> 00:23:55.030
Miki's already head over heels.

00:23:55.030 --> 00:23:58.040
<i>Anyway</i>... Doesn't Nagi look troubled?

00:23:58.040 --> 00:23:59.960
You're right. I wonder what's wrong?

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:02.310
And he finally had his Guardian Character hatch.

00:24:02.310 --> 00:24:03.880
I wonder if they got in a fight?

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:05.870
We've got to do something to help him!

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:06.410
Yeah!

00:24:06.410 --> 00:24:08.290
Rhythm is so cool...

00:24:08.290 --> 00:24:09.970
Miki...

00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:12.270
Next time on Shugo Chara!! Doki:

00:24:12.270 --> 00:24:14.390
It's Got to Be Cool! Beat Jumper!

00:24:14.390 --> 00:24:16.390
Oh, no! Nagi's about to faint!

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:17.780
Rhythm...

00:24:17.780 --> 00:24:19.560
And Miki's swooning!
